     1	# Delayed Market Making: Tail Characterization and Regret Rates
     2	
     3	We need solve the problem described in `latex/delays.tex`.
     4	
     5	Protocol:
     6	
     7	- At step `t`, the market reveals `P_t in [0,1]`.
     8	- The learner picks a quote `a_t in [0,1]`.
     9	- For all `t' < t`, if `a_{t'} < P_t`, then quote `a_{t'}` trades and earns reward `a_{t'}`.
    10	
    11	For a quote `a` posted at time `t`, define
    12	
    13	```tex
    14	\tau_t(a) := \min \{s > 0 : P_{t+s} > a\}.
    15	```
    16	
    17	The reward from posting quote `a` at time `t` over horizon `T` is
    18	
    19	```tex
    20	r_t(a) = a \mathbf 1\{\tau_t(a) \le T-t\}.
    21	```
    22	
    23	The regret is
    24	
    25	```tex
    26	R(T)
    27	=
    28	\max_{a \in [0,1]} \mathbb E\left[\sum_{t=1}^T r_t(a)\right]
    29	-
    30	\mathbb E\left[\sum_{t=1}^T r_t(a_t)\right].
    31	```
    32	
    33	The current conjectured tail condition is
    34	
    35	```tex
    36	\beta(h)
    37	:=
    38	\sup_t \sup_a
    39	\operatorname*{ess\,sup}_{P_1,\dots,P_t}
    40	\Pr\bigl[h < \tau_t(a) < \infty \mid P_1,\dots,P_t\bigr],
    41	```
    42	
    43	with assumption `lim_{h -> infinity} beta(h) = 0`.
