    23	## Lemma: Comparator-gap truncation comparison
    24	Status: proved
    25	Assumptions: Fixed exogenous price law \(P\); rewards \(r_t(a)\) and \(r_t^H(a)\) evaluated on the same price path; comparator uses \(\sup_a\).
    26	Statement: Define
    27	\[
    28	V_T=\sup_a\mathbb E\sum_{t=1}^T r_t(a),\qquad
    29	V_T^H=\sup_a\mathbb E\sum_{t=1}^T r_t^H(a),
    30	\]
    31	\[
    32	\delta_T(H)=V_T-V_T^H.
    33	\]
    34	For any learner,
    35	\[
    36	R_T\le R_T^H+\delta_T(H).
    37	\]
    38	Proof sketch: \(r_t^H(a_t)\le r_t(a_t)\) pathwise, so learner true reward is at least learner truncated reward. Then
    39	\[
    40	R_T=V_T-L_T\le V_T-L_T^H=(V_T^H-L_T^H)+(V_T-V_T^H).
    41	\]
