   108	## Lemma: Hidden-terminal two-world lower bound
   109	Status: proved for finite-horizon minimax class
   110	Assumptions: Horizon \(T=D+1\); learner does not know which of two laws in the class is active; the same learner must work for both.
   111	Statement: Let \(P_1=\cdots=P_D=0\). At terminal time set
   112	\[
   113	Y_L\sim\mathrm{Unif}[1/2,5/8],\qquad
   114	Y_H\sim\mathrm{Unif}[3/4,7/8].
   115	\]
   116	Then every randomized learner has regret at least \(D/8\) in one of the two worlds.
   117	Proof sketch: Before the terminal reveal, observations are identical. For \(g_i(a)=a\Pr(Y_i>a)\),
   118	\[
   119	V_L=1/2,\quad V_H=3/4,\quad \sup_a(g_L(a)+g_H(a))/2=1/2.
   120	\]
   121	The Bayes regret under a uniform prior is \(D((1/2+3/4)/2-1/2)=D/8\); apply Yao.
   122	Known gap: Does not imply a fixed-law asymptotic lower bound.
