   224	## Lemma: Grid-to-continuum minimax comparison
   225	Status: proved
   226	Assumptions: Public exogenous prices; arbitrary law class \(\Theta\); randomized measurable policies; continuum quote set \([0,1]\); grid \(G_K=\{0,1/K,\ldots,(K-1)/K\}\). Let \(\mathcal R_{[0,1]}\) and \(\mathcal R_{G_K}\) be the signed minimax regret values with matching learner/comparator action sets.
   227	Statement:
   228	\[
   229	|\mathcal R_{[0,1]}(\Theta,T)-\mathcal R_{G_K}(\Theta,T)|\le T/K.
   230	\]
   231	Proof sketch: Downward rounding satisfies, pathwise,
   232	\[
   233	a{\bf 1}\{M_t>a\}\le b{\bf 1}\{M_t>b\}+1/K,
   234	\]
   235	where \(b=\lfloor a\rfloor_K\in G_K\). This gives \(V_\theta\le V_\theta^{G_K}+T/K\), and hence \(\mathcal R_{[0,1]}\le \mathcal R_{G_K}+T/K\) by evaluating grid policies in the continuum game. Conversely, round every action of any continuum policy; the rounded grid policy loses at most \(T/K\) reward in every world, while \(V_\theta^{G_K}\le V_\theta\). Taking infima gives \(\mathcal R_{G_K}\le \mathcal R_{[0,1]}+T/K\).
   236	Known gaps: This does not define or prove an exact continuum \(\Psi\) formula; it only approximates continuum minimax values by grid minimax values.
   237	Source: `iterations/iter_005/solver_attempt.md`; iteration 5 critiques; `iterations/iter_008/idea_02/critic_01_on_explorer_01.md`; synthesis.
   238	
   239	## Lemma: Finite-class positive-part value equivalence
   240	Status: proved conditional on finite-grid minimax/Bayes identity and grid-to-continuum comparison
   241	Assumptions: Finite horizon-indexed public-exogenous class \(\Theta_T\); randomized measurable policies; continuum minimax signed upper-regret value \(\mathcal R_T^{[0,1]}\); grid \(G_T=\{0,1/T,\ldots,(T-1)/T\}\); grid Bayes value \(\sup_{\pi\in\Delta(\Theta_T)}\Psi_{G_T}(\pi)\).
   242	Statement:
   243	\[
   244	\left|
   245	(\mathcal R_T^{[0,1]})_+
   246	-
   247	\left(\sup_{\pi\in\Delta(\Theta_T)}\Psi_{G_T}(\pi)\right)_+
   248	\right|\le 1.
   249	\]
   250	Consequently,
   251	\[
   252	(\mathcal R_T^{[0,1]})_+=o(T)
   253	\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
   254	\left(\sup_{\pi\in\Delta(\Theta_T)}\Psi_{G_T}(\pi)\right)_+=o(T).
   255	\]
   256	Proof sketch: The finite-grid minimax/Bayes identity gives \(\mathcal R_T^{G_T}=\sup_\pi\Psi_{G_T}(\pi)\). The grid-to-continuum comparison gives \(|\mathcal R_T^{[0,1]}-\mathcal R_T^{G_T}|\le T/K=1\). Apply that \(x\mapsto x_+\) is 1-Lipschitz.
   257	Known gaps: Finite classes only. This is not an exact continuum least-favorable-prior formula, and it assumes the positive-part/upper-regret convention.
