    39	## Randomization is necessary for minimax/Bayes identities
    40	Construction: \(T=2\), \(P_1=0\), grid \(G=\{0.5,0.9\}\). Two worlds: in world 0, \(P_2=0.6\); in world 1, \(P_2=1\).
    41	Facts: The learner cannot distinguish worlds before choosing its only payoff-relevant quote. A deterministic learner choosing \(0.5\) has regrets \((0,0.4)\), and choosing \(0.9\) has regrets \((0.5,0)\), so deterministic minimax regret is \(0.4\). Randomizing with probability \(5/9\) on \(0.5\) balances regrets at \(2/9\).
